{"title":"2025 AIME I Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3(Fermat_Point)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3(Fermat Point)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_StressedPineapple\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by StressedPineapple</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/3/f13a96240c51d61ba3733d9f5c3020fa92ec4136.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" /> be a convex pentagon with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/c/7bc8e5a9b808e392d329c0e602c68435585f1585.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=14,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/c/6cc97a21acce68ef1542f17aae9726652dca0020.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=7,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/a/44acf5a602a0dff4739b45b456d03ea9ce3d57c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD=24,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/0/2e060fc03d88c1d4e49f35d5f9032b5acd97d81a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE=13,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/4/5c42e7f6f4823d589b6c14ca62200d210af3f4f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EA=26,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/7/d675357cc746dbcb2adf1a654d8f7414ad380195.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle B=\\angle E=60^{\\circ}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"136\" height=\"15\" /> For each point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> in the plane, define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/f/f2ff4f72dfa17950387fdae6d253c62363daba0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(X)=AX+BX+CX+DX+EX.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"316\" height=\"20\" /> The least possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/b/03b552622038cd329971eb0cba9465c82a2a3f03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(X)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"18\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/3482906f7af73d63aba487738a47c25254014f0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n\\sqrt{p},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"80\" height=\"21\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are positive integers and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is not divisible by the square of any prime. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/337be2d56c71c93d817fc635421ea2154bf992ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n+p.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"84\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/2/6920c4f5f74e0e89000fd11f348a11bc2bb4cd5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AX=a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"66\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/3/1b31d491392986e12a76d655708038b006824618.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BX=b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/9/d1904f1d0fbb61b0a2c0d2416992e3f1ab8fc3b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CX=c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/f/69fd9bc571447c586c88642a905cf920f7bb1765.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DX=d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"68\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/7/4c71e90fc1f74f884926d86d81eb7620b7a53b38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EX=e$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"14\" />, by Ptolemy inequality we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/3/ac3d35cbd64fe2767143d0d836b5fcb7a7d0b575.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+2d\\geq \\sqrt{3}XE; a+2c\\geq \\sqrt{3}BX$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"268\" height=\"23\" />, and as we are minimizing the value of the LHS, we want the inequality reached; this happens when both quadrilaterals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/7/d17e489160744ebf2eda3f87049e7522dc3ec49f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CXAB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/c/99c27140da4cbe9bc98a6e25a33304dd0acf31a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AXDE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"62\" height=\"14\" /> are concyclic. We notice that we have right angles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/f/88fe2523d90ff2e714897a59a0fbd0de500787b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{BXA}=\\angle{BCA}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"139\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/c/bec10ab152a54f4b2c207bd1d4e1fbddfdf7b827.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{EDA}=\\angle{EXA}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"140\" height=\"14\" /> as they both subtend a diameter of circles by noticing that we have formed Pythagorean triples (along with being told that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/8/3081e1e3235865c50039db2a92f0e2237b0ec7e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{B}=\\angle{E}=60^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"131\" height=\"15\" />. ）And so, since we have supplementary angles, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are collinear. Thus, we add up the two equalities to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/a/c0aa5e4afe7be82f62ebfa131212073d92584871.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a+2c+2d=\\sqrt{3}(XE+BX)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"247\" height=\"24\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/094cb8dcf81399c1fa0f60b99c97c2472601536a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+c+d=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}(BE)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"169\" height=\"43\" />. Thus we want to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/0/3c0c0d3d508ccfa6411bc98ef3b2cf8d071bb3e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c+d+e=(1+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})BE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"261\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p><p>By Law of Cosines, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/0/b70b658f772b7877856dbdf7c597f018ff143285.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(\\angle{DAC})=\\frac{1}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"134\" height=\"38\" />, and since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/f/c3f1df74e75cec6e8de49e45751bc276ed0d5cc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{CAB}=\\angle{DAE}=30^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"188\" height=\"15\" />, we know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302b6991f2d4f83c0256d3728523750ed123a68b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(\\angle{EAB})=cos(\\angle{CAB}+\\angle{DAE}+\\arccos(\\frac{1}{7}))=cos(60^{\\circ}+\\arccos(\\frac{1}{7}))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"579\" height=\"38\" />, which we find with the cosine angle addition formula and the fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/d/67dfdabf9bb455c4a0c3636493c95d2360566259.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(\\arccos(\\frac{1}{7}))=\\sqrt{1-(\\frac{1}{7})^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"222\" height=\"45\" />. Then, once again with Law of Cosines, we find  that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/d/a5df72377bb6c14107896b878dc8ff7eadf03c86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE=38$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />, and thus the minimum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/e/78e9da7691c4a59208721a2da0f7bbc510d639fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c+d+e$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"134\" height=\"16\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/f/58fdb23ea0e90e0174f14d041488931fc06bd90b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})BE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"105\" height=\"43\" />, is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/c/e5cbf48728673495ddbd0b2d1b96f5354850d93d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$38+19\\sqrt{3}\\implies\\boxed{060}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"173\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~Bluesoul ~hashbrown2009\n</p><p>Rewritten and edited by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Juwushu\" title=\"User:Juwushu\"> Juwushu</a>.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/8/048175e3e1f42b56af420a6cfb11020a4de51ac1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(10cm); import math; import geometry; import olympiad; point A,B,C,D,F,P,X; A=(0,-7sqrt(3)); B=(-7,0); C=(0,0); D=(156/7,-36sqrt(3)/7); F=(169/7,-88sqrt(3)/7); P=(132/7,60sqrt(3)/7); X=(8580/2527,-10604sqrt(3)/2527);  draw(A--B--C--P--D--F--A--C--D--A--P); draw(B--F); draw(circumcircle(A,B,C)); draw(circumcircle(A,D,F)); draw(circumcircle(C,P,D)); draw(C--X--D);  label(&quot;A&quot;,A,SE); label(&quot;B&quot;,B,W); label(&quot;C&quot;,C,NW); label(&quot;P&quot;,P,N); label(&quot;D&quot;,D,E); label(&quot;E&quot;,F,SE); label(&quot;X&quot;,X,E); [/asy]\" width=\"385\" height=\"475\" />\nFirstly, note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/0/db041d9c0fda44cf24b4f4ae7f02243ef2ea7f92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ADE$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> are just 30-60-90 triangles. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the Fermat point of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/7/0f7a55113a84ee4c04eb66f66d08310c32533ca2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ACD$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" />, with motivation stemming from considering the pentagon as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/7/0f7a55113a84ee4c04eb66f66d08310c32533ca2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ACD$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> with the two 30-60-90 extensions. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/a/4ca6375b3e314c0523e86cc41f49a9d32206227c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AX+CX+DX$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"139\" height=\"16\" /> is minimized at this point when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/8/e886a5faac85850d578bcec5b3883386b0e6f834.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AXC=\\angle CXD=\\angle AXD=120^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"284\" height=\"15\" />. Because we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/4/e942353454b3c1b57bc807228291921cfe46b3ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABC=\\angle AED=60^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"188\" height=\"15\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/c/dfc38365fa417b19e2aa8b3eea65805509f63af7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCX$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/c/99c27140da4cbe9bc98a6e25a33304dd0acf31a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AXDE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"62\" height=\"14\" /> are both cyclic. Then we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/3/4439b289edfab4f22aa14dcd7f54428356f608a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AXE=\\angle ADE=90^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"190\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/f/3ff83c20f26cf88e921682655c608272037f2765.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BXA=\\angle BCA=90^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"189\" height=\"15\" />. Then it turns out that we actually have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1abc88f38f8badb13ab2b68cdf1a3876e04ff5f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BXE=90^{\\circ}+90^{\\circ}=180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"218\" height=\"16\" />, implying that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are collinear. Now, by the triangle inequality, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/c/e4ccaca27f5da9f695a1ffb8fc0788b66a2fef21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BX+XE\\geq BE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"140\" height=\"17\" />, with equality occurring when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/b/a7baf95ecafc2d7791788ec79aeeae390d60b119.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/a/4ca6375b3e314c0523e86cc41f49a9d32206227c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AX+CX+DX$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"139\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/b/acb2788905b2ccba1fed8400a3990c86bec95e13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BX+EX$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"86\" height=\"16\" /> are minimized, so this point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is our desired point.\n</p><p>Firstly, we will find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/7/0a71a92193f643f27835ad8f8511803ff598a637.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BX+EX=BE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"140\" height=\"16\" />. We have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/4/f244b079d38c6cc77752f16b328ba1e8b7b5748d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=7\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"87\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/a/ada8127f9ba7d4287f4943143cfa20cb2dc2f69f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD=13\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"98\" height=\"21\" />, so applying the Law of Cosines in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/7/0f7a55113a84ee4c04eb66f66d08310c32533ca2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ACD$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/1/e912edd687c798efe688cae227d628a90c77a472.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[147+507-2(7\\sqrt{3})(13\\sqrt{3})\\cos (\\angle CAD)=576\\implies \\cos(\\angle CAD)=\\frac{1}{7}.\\]\" width=\"537\" height=\"37\" /> It follows as a result that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/7/9875765efea5e65d8fae087dd4f2c096c78641b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin (\\angle CAD)=\\frac{4\\sqrt{3}}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"156\" height=\"43\" />. Then we want to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/c/0cc972c0038dbb23a3649dceb0f70f4eec697b82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos (\\angle BAE)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"96\" height=\"20\" />. We can do this by seeing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/1/1319f364285dac0066cbe39e9b63ae9dbde260ba.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos (\\angle BAE)=\\cos (\\angle CAD+60^{\\circ})=\\cos (\\angle CAD)\\cos 60^{\\circ}-\\sin (\\angle CAD)\\sin 60^{\\circ}=\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{4\\sqrt{3}}{7}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}=-\\frac{11}{14}.\\]\" width=\"793\" height=\"41\" /> Applying the Law of Cosines again in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/9/1598bab45a40d37f82c1c831ca6c67965a273d47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BAE$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" />, then because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/3/f23446454eb9fccfe9b792aee481326e9a93c8b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=14$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/7/dc74c3bcc7bfec0ccf1082b3da061c7a40dddf5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE=26$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"14\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/b/98b9d57312463474b4e9b0538a700ad652420afb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[14^2+26^2-2(14)(26)\\left (-\\frac{11}{14}\\right )=196+676-2\\cdot 26\\cdot (-11)=872+572=1444=BE^2,\\]\" width=\"626\" height=\"43\" /> so it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/5/685810e369eaee4cb1e8af600c292e14935fdbb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE=38=BX+EX$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"182\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Now, we will find the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/a/4ca6375b3e314c0523e86cc41f49a9d32206227c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AX+CX+DX$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"139\" height=\"16\" />. Construct a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> outside such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/4/b243d29f35d19841f53b0d6f9fa338171ffefeb5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CPD$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> is equilateral, as shown. By property of fermat point, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are collinear. Additionally, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/8/678319fa03c799dc00389ef115f116c6c6b7c15f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CXD=120^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"120\" height=\"15\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/a/efab981cb0b6029f1e5ab128b71a1a076fb55d73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CPDX$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"62\" height=\"14\" /> is cyclic. Applying Ptolemy's Theorem, we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/7/d1799ed584f99f5d837d5ab75244b8a018196291.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(CX)(PD)+(CP)(XD)=(XP)(CD)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"315\" height=\"20\" />. But since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/4/b243d29f35d19841f53b0d6f9fa338171ffefeb5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CPD$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> is equilateral, it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/2/24284775bdcf9ed3466a9d60026fbfdab7869302.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CX+DX=PX$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"142\" height=\"16\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/b/4dbf2ebc3160be2a17e4bc888027a02488c3882b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AX+CX+DX=AX+PX=AP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"299\" height=\"16\" />, so we wish to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/b/e3bb4eeb347e74e025fd175c22f1f7275af0555e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. Applying the Law of Cosines in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/7/0f7a55113a84ee4c04eb66f66d08310c32533ca2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ACD$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" />, we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/1/2d14ad4b715e578d5e2fcfdd20d494aa57779c7f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(13\\sqrt{3})^2+24^2-2(13\\sqrt{3})(24)\\cos (\\angle ADC)=(7\\sqrt{3})^2\\implies \\cos (\\angle ADC)=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\implies \\angle ADC=30^{\\circ}.\\]\" width=\"747\" height=\"41\" /> Then because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6ef981ae67bf9aa6d89ed58529e8a419e5830e70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CDP=60^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"109\" height=\"15\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/4/944303920f4fa900fe7a9967e0e841222c5259d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ADP=90^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"108\" height=\"15\" />, so we can find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/b/e3bb4eeb347e74e025fd175c22f1f7275af0555e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> simply with the Pythagorean Theorem. We know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/a/ada8127f9ba7d4287f4943143cfa20cb2dc2f69f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD=13\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"98\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/b/91bb154ddb50abea7815f10b369e2b6cd98bc348.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DP=CD=24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"128\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/e/b3e14b92dcaf8783e320c312a9be20c40c8174d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP=\\sqrt{(13\\sqrt{3})^2+24^2}=19\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -9px\" width=\"250\" height=\"35\" />.\n</p><p>We then have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/c/2dc4537e4cef7fd6ed5f917fa70052a88840074c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(X)=AX+BX+CX+DX+EX=(BX+EX)+(AX+CX+DX)=BE+AP=38+19\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"819\" height=\"24\" />, which is our minimum value. Therefore, the answer to the problem is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/c/1ec07756105b1275ea970438b0569e72596c68bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$38+19+3=\\boxed{060}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"155\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~ethanzhang1001\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3.28Fermat_Point.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3(Fermat_Point)\">Solution 3(Fermat Point)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3(Fermat Point)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/e/bdeb53ae928cecf320a91122a95e651cc4da154d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE = 26$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/7/1e7fe5ddb45225d87ff6686c2ec06aa75ee87fdd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE = 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/7/9974642e6d63ee8906ad67ec7cda4dca784b41b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{E}={60}^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"79\" height=\"15\" />, which means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/f/94fd708ca38949d7f031621a87de383a4b789f20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{AED}$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> is a 30-60-90 triangle, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/5/63513c7e90d0e4608d0acd1a70b2132feebbafa5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = 13\\sqrt3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"98\" height=\"21\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/a/88afad887048299164d291c5dabcbc7e0ca9f091.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{EAD}={30}^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"108\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/5/d2594c0857ed7f3b8944cc810432ec46c3501acb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{ADE}={90}^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"108\" height=\"15\" />. Similar with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/8/1f828f10cad9235a2c72c34369f5fd4a1179e579.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{ABC}$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/a/d8ae6b0ffa439b9e7a798dfd747c5b8e5e99f4a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = 7\\sqrt3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"89\" height=\"21\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/a/48a6eca71bf35f82f72de4c3f236f9d7203f76ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{BAC}={30}^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/5/5d515489fa70eaddb17c1d9d54a76eeefefe7d47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{ACB}={90}^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>To solve the question, we would have to locate point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> first. We first consider the points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. For the distance of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to become the shortest, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> should lay on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/b/a7baf95ecafc2d7791788ec79aeeae390d60b119.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> to be closest to point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, it should be on the foot of perpendicular from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/b/a7baf95ecafc2d7791788ec79aeeae390d60b119.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>Consider about <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/c/fcceaba30513d600247e1b940cada47f0689d333.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{ADE}=\\angle{AXE}={90}^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"190\" height=\"15\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/c/99c27140da4cbe9bc98a6e25a33304dd0acf31a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AXDE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"62\" height=\"14\" /> is cyclic. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/f/d8f762b4975e642ddd062dad623c76dc54241545.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{EXD}=\\angle{EAD}=\\angle{BXC}={30}^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"275\" height=\"15\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/4/11464c9709aaa34bc840dfdf7fc2a570fdaf1d62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{DXC}=\\angle{AXD}=\\angle{AXD}={120}^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"286\" height=\"15\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is coincidently the Fermat Point of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840cb55c82434b9ae047760636a017e9441e6ca5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>To calculate the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/b/03b552622038cd329971eb0cba9465c82a2a3f03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(X)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"18\" />, we divide it into 2 parts: the sum of distance to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and the sum of distance to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Applying Ptolemy's Theorem in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/c/99c27140da4cbe9bc98a6e25a33304dd0acf31a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AXDE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"62\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/f/94f0b5f72f3f8b24c95016247b0b4ab2b57ba94e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AXCB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"14\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/e/84e3f64e8d287a0ca10a86826f5273202e36f1d4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AX+2DX=\\sqrt3EX\\]\" width=\"171\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/8/898635a7fa5f3c497e525cb4ee17d5708b42a81b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[and\\]\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/d/b4de82102d16ebfc2ea6759130f2269ac01e1f0f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AX+2CX=\\sqrt3BX\\]\" width=\"170\" height=\"18\" />\nWe get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/b/adbc8afbcb68c4975badbfe6e67bb2cc2c48ad3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AX+DX+CX = \\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\cdot(EX+BX) = \\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}BE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"385\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Construct equilateral triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/a/acad5629f89ba033c79d7d59d7c0605d2a5cac48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{ADE}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> outside of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/e/86e64c54cb966e2c0cd008ac8ce27b258fa5ff53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{ADC}$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> on side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />. Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is the Fermat Point, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/6/6b69d427c9edadc358dc4ac2a3d933ef1c37b82c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FC=AX+DX+CX$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"192\" height=\"16\" />. To calculate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/e/f1e715454d4a9ea7decd4afc39bb1630bdf82ad4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FC$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />, we needed to utilize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/2/4b2a4522f4bd4ae9044e2eecb4a4a3ae673857a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{FDC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"59\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/a/a7a89b6ab1b510a263b01fce65e8ed6ee53b3533.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle{FDC}=\\angle{FDA}+\\angle{ADC}={60}^{\\circ}+\\angle{ADC}\\]\" width=\"344\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>From <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/e/86e64c54cb966e2c0cd008ac8ce27b258fa5ff53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{ADC}$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" />, we know:\n\\begin{align*}\n\\cos{\\angle{ADC}} &amp; = \\frac{(13\\sqrt3)^2+{24}^2-(7\\sqrt3)^2}{2\\cdot13\\sqrt3\\cdot24}\\\\\n&amp;= \\frac{936}{2\\cdot13\\sqrt3\\cdot24}\\\\\n&amp;= \\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\\\\n\\end{align*}\n</p><p>This shows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/5/8f5e809566b3ff82432a6aa0a4d600cc6cea9d44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{ADC} = {30}^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"108\" height=\"15\" />, which means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/1/bd160f3a07de6e9d498a68b0f5ec9624f780d07e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{FDC} = {60}^{\\circ}+{30}^{\\circ}={90}^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"207\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Using the Pythagorean Theorem,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/c/55c8bb97ab3d6d7d48248f22e39ad38050e658d4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[FC = \\sqrt{(13\\sqrt3)^2+24^2)}=19\\sqrt3=AX+DX+CD\\]\" width=\"416\" height=\"32\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/f/83f159ec3948d80d17374af38c7e1167f96b474d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(X) = 19\\sqrt3(1+\\frac{2}{\\sqrt3})=38+19\\sqrt3\\]\" width=\"289\" height=\"41\" /> \n</p><p>The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/c/1ec07756105b1275ea970438b0569e72596c68bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$38+19+3=\\boxed{060}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"155\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~cassphe\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_StressedPineapple\">Video Solution 1 by StressedPineapple</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by StressedPineapple\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtube.com/watch?v=ttQrUg6A4PA&amp;t=334s\">https://youtube.com/watch?v=ttQrUg6A4PA&amp;t=334s</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://youtu.be/1_5sBJDVi1I?si=atCuCeA2eeSmkEav\">2025 AIME I #14</a>\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://mathproblemsolvingskills.wordpress.com/\">MathProblemSolvingSkills.com</a>\n</p><p>Great solution!\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I\" title=\"2025 AIME I\">2025 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2025 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2025 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2025\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2025 AIME I Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2025 AIME I Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2025 AIME I Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2025 AIME I Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2025 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2025 AIME I Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2025 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2025 AIME I Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2025 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2025 AIME I Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2025 AIME I Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2025 AIME I Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2025 AIME I Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2025 AIME I Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2025 AIME I Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2025 AIME I Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018030815\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.076 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.099 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 868/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1790/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 112/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐exp